==Trivia==
*Starting with the thirtieth call, Yancy's sprite will begin to blush when talking on the Xtransceiver, implying she has developed feelings for the male player, just like her male counterpart, [[Curtis]], has for the female player.
*The Pokémon traded to Yancy by the player can occasionally appear with her in her various television shows.
**If she is traded a Pokémon that can [[evolve]] when traded, however, it will not evolve upon being traded to her and will remain its original species.
**Similarly, if she is traded a [[nickname]]d Pokémon, the television will instead display its species name. 
*Yancy will occasionally talk about other regions, which she has visited on business trips: [[Kanto]], [[Johto]], [[Hoenn]], and [[Sinnoh]]. This list includes every region that appears in the [[core series]] prior to [[Generation V]].
**She has unique dialogue for each of these regions and will trade the player a Pokémon that was originally discovered in the mentioned region and is holding the region's [[Pokémon food#Local specialty|local specialty]]. For example, if she mentions Hoenn, she will trade the player a {{p|Ralts}}, {{p|Mawile}}, or {{p|Spinda}} that is holding a [[Lava Cookie]].
***Excluding Kanto, she will mention the local specialty in her dialogue about the region.

